net: Add SOCKS5 username/password authentication

Chromium's SOCKS5 client offers only "no authentication", so a proxy
that requires a username and password cannot be used, and Chromium's
proxy configuration has no place for the credentials.

Implement RFC 1929 in SOCKS5ClientSocket: with credentials, the
greeting offers username/password besides no authentication, and if
the proxy picks it, the sub-negotiation runs before the CONNECT
request; rejected credentials fail with the new ERR_SOCKS_AUTH_FAILED
(-185, a retired number). The credentials come from a lookup function
the embedder registers, which SOCKSConnectJob calls with the proxy it
connected to. Without one the client behaves exactly as before.

Builds on 0002-net-Tell-SOCKS5-failures-apart.patch.

